{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggLHLNyAwmbnngSn4FPQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The grosz leak in `split_cents` is fixed. `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, and the shares always sum to the total.\n\n- **Cause:** the function used floor division for every share and dropped the remainder.\n- **Fix (`money.py`):** the remainder is spread one grosz at a time over the first people, so no grosz is lost.\n- **Tests (`test_money.py`):** I added a test for `[34, 33, 33]` and a property check that shares sum to the total and differ by at most one, for totals 0–499 and 1–11 people. I ran both before the fix and they failed, then they passed after it.\n\n`python3 -m unittest test_money` passes all 5 tests. I did not run the full suite, and I did not commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":774,"cache_read_input_tokens":22072,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":774},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cdd4ccf-e3e0-406e-8a5f-ae0cdd13998e","uuid":"dbd5a946-fe46-43b6-ba71-5f8a1766d28a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T16:45:56.455Z","request_id":"req_011CggLHL8bS9Uckwd8JUDEd"}
